}, {"t": " (", "lp": -0.004085291177034378, "top": [[" (", -0.004085291177034378], [" on", -6.394389629364014]]}, {"t": "av", "lp": -2.605748414993286, "top": [["not", -1.025199294090271], ["important", -1.7021076679229736]]}, {"t": "oids", "lp": -6.6757424974639434e-06, "top": [["oids", -6.6757424974639434e-06], ["oid", -12.580584526062012]]}, {"t": " `/", "lp": -0.936314046382904, "top": [[" `/", -0.936314046382904], [" the", -1.0983775854110718]]}, {"t": "usr", "lp": -0.00026927044382318854, "top": [["usr", -0.00026927044382318854], ["lib", -8.546545028686523]]}, {"t": "/lib", "lp": -0.0008101764251478016, "top": [["/lib", -0.0008101764251478016], ["/x", -7.586917400360107]]}], "text": "# PKGBUILD `build()` Function: Step-by-Step Explanation\n\nLet me break down this `build()` function flag by flag.\n\n## Setup Commands\n\n```bash\nsource /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh --force\n```\nThis loads the Intel oneAPI environment variables (compiler paths, library paths, etc.) into the current shell. The `--force` flag overwrites any existing environment. Without this, `icx`/`icpx` won't be found.\n\n```bash\nset -e\n```\nExit immediately if any command returns a non-zero status. This is standard in build functions to catch failures early.\n\n## The CMake Configuration Command\n\n```bash\ncmake -S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\" -B \"${srcdir}/build\" -G Ninja \\\n```\n- **`-S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\"`** \u2014 Source directory (where the CMakeLists.txt lives). Note this points to the *extracted git repo*, not a separate source.\n- **`-B \"${srcdir}/build\"`** \u2014 Build directory (out-of-source build).\n- **`-G Ninja`** \u2014 Use the Ninja build system (fast, mentioned in `makedepends`).\n\n## Build Type and Install Paths\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \\\n```\nOptimization flags enabled (`-O3` typically). This is *not* Debug (no `-g`), consistent with the `!debug` option.\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr -DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib \\\n```\n- **`-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr`** \u2014 Install location.\n- **`-DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib`** \u2014 Libraries go to `/usr/lib` (avoids `/usr/lib"}